3. Creating the Enterprise GitHub Automation Pipeline
Whenever your development team pushes edits or updates system valuation parameters on GitHub, this automation script (.github/workflows/deploy-infrastructure.yml) acts as your automated gatekeeper. It locks secrets safely away, runs a compliance build, and readies your application container:

name: Production Ledger Automation Pipeline
on:
  push:
    branches: [ main ] # Automatically triggers execution on your main branch
jobs:
  build_and_verify:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
    - name: Access Codebase Repository
      uses: actions/checkout@v4

    - name: Initialize Docker Build Environment
      uses: docker/setup-buildx-action@v3

    - name: Audit Code Security Parameters
      run: |
        echo "Scanning codebase for hardcoded cryptographic keys or secrets..."
        # Your developers can insert automated security linting tools here
    - name: Compile Enterprise Container Node
      uses: docker/build-push-action@v5
      with:
        context: .
        push: false # Set to true once your target host registry secrets are linked
        tags: dhcsoln/ledger-engine:v3.0.0


